WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.463 --> 00:00:02.640
- Good morning, Believe
Nation, my name is Lily,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.586
and my one word is extraordinary.

00:00:04.586 --> 00:00:06.819
I live to encourage people
to be extraordinary,

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:09.942
so together we can make this
world an extraordinary place.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.689
So to help you on your
journey, today's message is

00:00:12.689 --> 00:00:15.817
attack over to you, John Jocko Willink,

00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:18.275
(rooster cawing)

00:00:18.275 --> 00:00:20.768
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.768 --> 00:00:23.070
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.570
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:30.385
- One of my direct subordinates,

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:31.974
one of my guys that worked for me,

00:00:31.974 --> 00:00:34.416
he would call me up or pull me aside

00:00:34.416 --> 00:00:38.241
with some major problem,
some issue that was going on.

00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:40.667
And he'd saw, boss we got this
and that and the other thing.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.957
And I'd look at him and I'd say, good.

00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:46.556
And finally one day he was
telling me about some issue

00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:48.390
that he was having, some problem,

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.544
and he said, I already know
what you're going to say.

00:00:51.544 --> 00:00:53.597
And I say, well what am I going to say?

00:00:53.597 --> 00:00:57.151
He said, you're going to say good.

00:00:57.151 --> 00:00:58.977
He said, that's what you always say.

00:00:58.977 --> 00:01:01.784
When something is wrong and going bad,

00:01:01.784 --> 00:01:05.676
you always just look at me and say good.

00:01:05.676 --> 00:01:07.479
And I said, well yeah.

00:01:07.479 --> 00:01:11.646
When things are going bad,
there's going to be some good

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.253
that's going to come from it.

00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:18.103
Didn't get the new high
speed gear we wanted?

00:01:18.103 --> 00:01:19.387
Good.

00:01:19.387 --> 00:01:21.042
Didn't get promoted?

00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:25.205
Good, more time to get better.

00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:27.304
Oh, mission got canceled?

00:01:27.304 --> 00:01:29.182
Good, we can focus on our other one.

00:01:29.182 --> 00:01:30.672
Didn't get funded?

00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:32.841
Didn't get the job you wanted?

00:01:32.841 --> 00:01:35.954
Got injured, sprained my
ankle, got tapped out?

00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:37.183
Good.

00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:38.471
Got beat?

00:01:38.471 --> 00:01:42.498
Good, you learned.

00:01:42.498 --> 00:01:44.771
Unexpected problems?

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:48.938
Good, we have the opportunity
to figure out a solution.

00:01:50.714 --> 00:01:53.797
That's it, when things are going bad,

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.205
don't get all bummed out,

00:01:56.205 --> 00:02:00.038
don't get startled, don't get frustrated.

00:02:02.177 --> 00:02:05.760
If you can say the word
"good," guess what?

00:02:08.487 --> 00:02:10.857
It means you're still alive.

00:02:10.857 --> 00:02:13.371
It means you're still breathing.

00:02:13.371 --> 00:02:17.204
And if you're still
breathing, well then hell,

00:02:18.184 --> 00:02:21.066
you still got some fight left in you.

00:02:21.066 --> 00:02:25.233
So get up, dust off, reload,

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:30.968
recalibrate, reengage.

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:36.563
And go out on the attack.

00:02:36.563 --> 00:02:39.419
- So I think too many
people dwell on the bad,

00:02:39.419 --> 00:02:40.756
and not on the good.

00:02:40.756 --> 00:02:43.739
They get so consumed about the
current situation they're in

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:45.262
and they complain,

00:02:45.262 --> 00:02:48.386
without realizing that
they could do so much more.

00:02:48.386 --> 00:02:52.441
I think about my situation,
I grew up really poor.

00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:56.608
I slept on the floor in a tiny
room that my parents rented.

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:00.447
I wasn't able to go on
any trips with my friends.

00:03:00.447 --> 00:03:02.612
I wasn't able to buy the fancy clothes.

00:03:02.612 --> 00:03:05.574
I was made fun of because
my pants were too short.

00:03:05.574 --> 00:03:07.743
But you know what, I'm grateful.

00:03:07.743 --> 00:03:10.321
I'm grateful for all those experiences.

00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:12.721
Because it made me who I am today.

00:03:12.721 --> 00:03:15.412
I wouldn't be 25% of the person I am today

00:03:15.412 --> 00:03:17.954
if I hadn't gone through
all those hardships.

00:03:17.954 --> 00:03:22.065
I wouldn't have known how to
work hard, to be resourceful.

00:03:22.065 --> 00:03:24.281
I know the pain and
the struggle that comes

00:03:24.281 --> 00:03:28.623
from not having money, and
it made me work so hard.

00:03:28.623 --> 00:03:32.491
I would wake up every Saturday
when I was 13 years old

00:03:32.491 --> 00:03:36.151
at 5am so I could go
work a waitress shift,

00:03:36.151 --> 00:03:37.985
while everybody else slept.

00:03:37.985 --> 00:03:40.873
I knew everything I wanted
wasn't going to be given to me.

00:03:40.873 --> 00:03:42.918
I knew I had to work hard for it.

00:03:42.918 --> 00:03:44.224
So everything that I do today,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.837
whether it's a job that I want,

00:03:45.837 --> 00:03:47.331
the business I want to create,

00:03:47.331 --> 00:03:50.762
being in front of the camera
right now, it's all hard work.

00:03:50.762 --> 00:03:52.347
And nobody sees that,

00:03:52.347 --> 00:03:55.048
people see the opportunities
that I've given to people,

00:03:55.048 --> 00:03:58.091
but they don't see the hard
work that goes behind it.

00:03:58.091 --> 00:04:00.998
So next time you find yourself
complaining about something,

00:04:00.998 --> 00:04:02.986
you not having the right equipment,

00:04:02.986 --> 00:04:05.656
not being the right gender,
not being the right color,

00:04:05.656 --> 00:04:07.395
not having the right contacts,

00:04:07.395 --> 00:04:11.547
think about what is right
about you and focus on that.

00:04:11.547 --> 00:04:13.534
Because that's your strength.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.839
That is what's going to make
you grow and become stronger,

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:18.759
and that will make you unique
and become the person you are.

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:21.306
So next time you're facing
a difficult situation,

00:04:21.306 --> 00:04:24.255
think to yourself, "good" and attack.

00:04:24.255 --> 00:04:25.681
So the question of the day is,

00:04:25.681 --> 00:04:28.818
what is the bad situation
you're dealing with right now?

00:04:28.818 --> 00:04:30.338
So leave it in the comments below,

00:04:30.338 --> 00:04:32.026
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:04:32.026 --> 00:04:33.952
I also have a quick shout
out for Andy Duinker.

00:04:33.952 --> 00:04:35.548
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:04:35.548 --> 00:04:37.163
of Evan's book, "Your One Word."

00:04:37.163 --> 00:04:38.677
Your support means a lot to us

00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:40.558
and we hope you're enjoying the read,

00:04:40.558 --> 00:04:42.246
So thank you so much for watching,

00:04:42.246 --> 00:04:45.194
we believe in you and hope
you continue to believe

00:04:45.194 --> 00:04:47.462
in yourself and whatever your one word is.

00:04:47.462 --> 00:04:49.094
And we'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:49.094 --> 00:04:52.761
for another shot of espresso.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.951
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:57.951 --> 00:05:01.651
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:01.651 --> 00:05:03.734
(typing)

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.207
- If there's anything in life

00:05:06.207 --> 00:05:08.120
that you don't currently have right now,

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.866
it's because of who you
are and how you think.

00:05:10.866 --> 00:05:13.348
Come on, right now, you saying
ET man, you talking to me.

00:05:13.348 --> 00:05:15.019
Man, I'm going through some type of pain,

00:05:15.019 --> 00:05:16.977
I'm ready to quit and give
up, let me see your hand.

00:05:16.977 --> 00:05:18.468
I'm ready to quit and give
up, let me see your hand.

00:05:18.468 --> 00:05:20.206
Something in life, I'm ready
to quit on, give up on.

00:05:20.206 --> 00:05:21.427
Come on, raise your hand high.

00:05:21.427 --> 00:05:23.043
I'm ready to quit on, I'm
ready to give up on it,

00:05:23.043 --> 00:05:23.876
come on raise it up.

00:05:23.876 --> 00:05:24.899
Alright, what I need you to do is

00:05:24.899 --> 00:05:26.561
I need you to find a reason to keep going.

00:05:26.561 --> 00:05:27.906
And if you can find a
reason to keep going,

00:05:27.906 --> 00:05:29.177
I know you're strong enough to do it.

00:05:29.177 --> 00:05:32.233
Cause you human, and every
human has what it takes

00:05:32.233 --> 00:05:34.199
to get past whatever they going through

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.745
if they decide to.

00:05:36.745 --> 00:05:40.039
Push through it, push through it.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:42.300
Tragedy and trials come to everybody.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.864
Only the strong survive.

00:05:44.864 --> 00:05:47.391
I watch my wife when she got diagnosed,

00:05:47.391 --> 00:05:49.388
I watched my wife have terrible days.

00:05:49.388 --> 00:05:51.470
And she probably missed two days of work

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.956
the whole time she had MS.

00:05:52.956 --> 00:05:54.554
I watched her go to work and I'm like,

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.710
boo, why in the world would
you get up and go to work?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:00.199
You don't even need the money.

00:06:00.199 --> 00:06:02.599
Why would you do it, it's cold.

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:04.221
It's 10 degrees in Michigan

00:06:04.221 --> 00:06:07.691
and your MS flare up when
it's cold, what are you doing.

00:06:07.691 --> 00:06:09.204
She said, I can't see my daughter,

00:06:09.204 --> 00:06:12.701
I can't have my daughter see me weak.

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:14.796
Cause my daughter going
to be married one day,

00:06:14.796 --> 00:06:16.937
and my daughter going
to face tragedy one day,

00:06:16.937 --> 00:06:19.663
and I have to show her how to do it.

00:06:19.663 --> 00:06:22.588
So I get up and get dressed,
and I go to work every day,

00:06:22.588 --> 00:06:26.050
so my baby girl can know
how to get through trials.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.953
Cause one day she ain't
going to be under our roof,

00:06:28.953 --> 00:06:31.122
and she going to have to do it alone.

00:06:31.122 --> 00:06:32.398
And I don't want to talk,

00:06:32.398 --> 00:06:35.949
I want to model what it looks like.

00:06:35.949 --> 00:06:37.442
My daughter got on the prayer line,

00:06:37.442 --> 00:06:39.174
she could pray me another
day, told her testimony,

00:06:39.174 --> 00:06:40.889
she's like, I didn't even
feel like going to school,

00:06:40.889 --> 00:06:43.006
I didn't feel like walking
a mile to go to class.

00:06:43.006 --> 00:06:46.761
And I thought about it, my
mom got a chronic illness.

00:06:46.761 --> 00:06:49.716
My mom, in her 40s, could
get up with a chronic illness

00:06:49.716 --> 00:06:51.476
and go to work, why surely I can get up

00:06:51.476 --> 00:06:55.141
at 18 years old and go to class.

00:06:55.141 --> 00:06:59.308
It worked, it worked, it worked!

00:07:00.171 --> 00:07:04.161
Listen to me very closely, you
all running from obstacles,

00:07:04.161 --> 00:07:05.898
when in fact it's the obstacle

00:07:05.898 --> 00:07:07.593
that's going to take
you to the next level.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:11.297
Like you all running from pain,
you all running from challenges.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.289
You telling me how difficult your life is,

00:07:13.289 --> 00:07:15.478
do you understand it is the difficulty

00:07:15.478 --> 00:07:18.801
that's going to prepare you and
take you to that next level?

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:21.233
Why do you keep crying, why me, God?

00:07:21.233 --> 00:07:23.631
Why did I get MS, why did I get cancer,

00:07:23.631 --> 00:07:26.321
why did my mama die, why did I get fired?

00:07:26.321 --> 00:07:29.637
Do you understand, list
you got through that,

00:07:29.637 --> 00:07:32.205
you got put through that,
because what that does,

00:07:32.205 --> 00:07:34.611
that tension produces greatness.

00:07:34.611 --> 00:07:36.715
Stop running from it and run to it.

00:07:36.715 --> 00:07:38.465
Come on you all, you all got to hear me.

00:07:38.465 --> 00:07:40.151
The reason why you do what you do

00:07:40.151 --> 00:07:42.297
is more critical than what you do.

00:07:42.297 --> 00:07:44.152
And if why you do what you do is weak,

00:07:44.152 --> 00:07:46.413
I need you to go back
and start all over again.

00:07:46.413 --> 00:07:48.362
Because if your reasoning is weak,

00:07:48.362 --> 00:07:49.738
you're not going to get it done.

00:07:49.738 --> 00:07:52.454
Why, because life is going
to beat you upside your head.

00:07:52.454 --> 00:07:53.466
And I'm going to tell you this,

00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:55.080
I don't care who you are
and what profession you in,

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:58.195
before you blow up, life
will strip you to the core.

00:07:58.195 --> 00:08:00.055
But if you weak, you will be broke.

00:08:00.055 --> 00:08:01.773
And I'm not here because I'm the best.

00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:05.213
I'm here because they tried to
break me, and they couldn't.

00:08:05.213 --> 00:08:06.859
- Guy just hit me on Snapchat and said,

00:08:06.859 --> 00:08:11.441
hey man, I'm going for it cause
I only got one life to live.

00:08:11.441 --> 00:08:13.844
And I Snapped him back and just said,

00:08:13.844 --> 00:08:18.306
hey man, what if that one
life thing isn't true, bro?

00:08:18.306 --> 00:08:19.979
And now he's wondering, he's like,

00:08:19.979 --> 00:08:21.238
what you mean, man, what you mean?

00:08:21.238 --> 00:08:23.743
I said, well here's the deal, okay?

00:08:23.743 --> 00:08:26.072
I mean you don't know
and I don't know, right?

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:28.623
I mean maybe you don't
know, and maybe I do.

00:08:28.623 --> 00:08:32.280
But here's the deal.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.558
I'm much more dangerous and
much more of a risk taker

00:08:35.558 --> 00:08:39.725
and much more a go-it-all-the-way
dude and less introverted

00:08:40.874 --> 00:08:45.609
when I'm not worried about
the one life myth, okay.

00:08:45.609 --> 00:08:49.390
I'm thinking, hey baby,
what if I live forever, man?

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.203
Then am I willing to take the risk,

00:08:51.203 --> 00:08:53.226
am I willing to make the sales call?

00:08:53.226 --> 00:08:57.815
See, me living forever,
the immortality concept,

00:08:57.815 --> 00:09:01.885
makes me way dangerous,
makes me sick dangerous,

00:09:01.885 --> 00:09:05.639
makes me crazy dangerous, okay.

00:09:05.639 --> 00:09:09.513
It makes me want to go for
it every freaking single day

00:09:09.513 --> 00:09:12.300
because I don't have the ultimate to lose.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.001
You understand what I'm saying?

00:09:14.001 --> 00:09:15.687
Hey, check it out, maybe you know,

00:09:15.687 --> 00:09:18.893
maybe you don't know,
but I bet you're curious.

00:09:18.893 --> 00:09:20.417
What if you live forever?

00:09:20.417 --> 00:09:22.060
What if this like the thousandth time?

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.348
What if you've got a thousand
more runs at this deal?

00:09:24.348 --> 00:09:25.761
Well then go for it.

00:09:25.761 --> 00:09:27.774
Bottom line is one life or many lives,

00:09:27.774 --> 00:09:30.280
go for it today, go for it in a big way,

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:33.204
and go for it like you
going to live forever.

